# How long SC0000's page 13->14 transition takes. The click runs label_1235a four times, each ending in an op-0x21c
# effect wait (run-state 0x400): native's own clock times them at 150, 890, 150 and 300 ms, and page 14's show-text
# runs about 1.5 s after the click. The checks are coarse, for the driver's own latency: the effects still run half a
# second after the click, and page 14's text wait is reached within about 2.3 s of it. Both targets reveal page 14's
# 31 glyphs in about 160 ms first: native reaches the wait 1.66 s after the click, the port about 1.72 s.
#
# Setting system:EffectSkipOnClick 0, a new profile's default, so nothing skips the effects.
#
# Run on a fresh sandbox, on both targets:
#   py -3.11 -X utf8 tools/drive.py port start
#   py -3.11 -X utf8 tools/drive.py port run tools/drive/scenarios/himegari-effect-waits.steps

wait-state script=TITLE click=adv.next every=3 timeout=120   # click through the logos and opening movie
wait 1.5
click title.start
wait-state script=GAMESTART timeout=20
wait 1
click newgame.begin
wait-state top=SC0000@0x83f timeout=60  # page 1
settle timeout=20
advance 12
settle timeout=20
expect top=SC0000@0xc04                 # page 13
move 400 300
wait 1

click adv.next hold=20                  # page 13 -> 14
wait 0.5
expect top=SC0000@0x123df               # still in the effect waits (the second, 890 ms)
wait-state top=SC0000@0xe0f timeout=1.6 # page 14's text wait (op 0x72 at 0xe0c)
shot effect-waits-page14
